# (0.17.61) SONG MODE THAT SOUNDS ARRANGED: a place that brings the drums in is built up to: a build over the last bars of the place before (the genre's
# length, at most half the place; the drums of a place without them come in for it), the drop on the new place's first bar. A place that leaves the drums
# out comes in as a breakdown. Anything else: the fill, as before.
seed 0
wait 3000
tap GLO
wait 100
tap GLO
wait 100
expect view 34
# place 1: HYPNO 01, 8 bars, no drums
spin K2 1
spin K3 2
tapkey 10
wait 100
expect setbars0 8
expect setmute0 16
# place 2: HYPNO 03, 8 bars, everything
spin K1 1
spin K2 1
spin K2 2
spin K3 2
wait 100
expect setsl1 3
expect setbars1 8
expect setmute1 0
# place 3: HYPNO 03, 4 bars, no drums
spin K1 1
spin K2 1
spin K2 2
spin K3 1
tapkey 10
wait 100
expect setbars2 4
expect setmute2 16
# Play: Loop, from the top
spin K4 1
wait 100
expect seton 1
expect setend 0
tap PLAY
wait 300
tap PLAY
wait 200
expect setpos 0
expect trkmute 15
expect sec 0
# place 1's last four bars: the build, the drums in for it
waitfor setbar 4 30000
wait 300
expect sec 2
expect trkmute 0
# place 2: the drop
waitfor setpos 1 30000
wait 600
expect sec 0
expect trkmute 0
# place 3: a breakdown
waitfor setpos 2 30000
wait 600
expect sec 1
expect trkmute 15
# round to place 1 (no drums to no drums: still down), then its build again from the breakdown, and the drop
waitfor setpos 0 30000
wait 600
expect sec 1
waitfor setbar 4 30000
wait 300
expect sec 2
waitfor setpos 1 30000
wait 600
expect sec 0
